---
name: YAML to register map (Markdown)
format: markdown
---
{#-
  yaml-to-register-map.j2 — BACKWARD template: open a *_fpga_types.yaml
  (the output of the register-map-to-* templates) and press Generate: it
  converts the data back into a register-map Markdown document (one-line
  register rows, prose descriptions and nested field/enum tables).

  Reconstruction assumptions (the data file is a lossy projection):
  - every register is 32 bit, at sequential 4-byte offsets (word = index);
  - field offsets are recomputed cumulatively from the field sizes;
  - a field named "<register>_padding" is written back as "reserved";
  - the struct section and codegen blocks are not part of the document.
-#}
{%- if not types %}
This document is not a register map: it needs a "types:" section (YAML or JSON).
{%- else %}
| Offset | Word | Name | Size | Format | Access | Description |
| ------ | ---- | --------------- | ------ | -------- | ------ | ----------- |
{% for name, t in types | items %}
{%- if t.format != 'struct' -%}{{ "\n" if loop.index0 > 0 else "" }}| {{ loop.index0 * 4 }} | {{ loop.index0 }} | {{ name }} | {{ t | size_display }} | {{ t.format }} | {{ t.fpga.flags | access_display }} | {{ t | array_suffix }} |
{%- if t.doc %}

{{ t.doc | esc_md }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if t.format == 'enum' %}

| Value | Name |
| ----- | --------- |
{% for vname, v in t.values | items -%}
| {{ v }} | {{ vname | esc_md }} |
{% endfor %}
{%- elif t.format == 'bitfield' %}

| Offset | Name | Size | Type | Description |
| ------ | --------- | ------ | ---- | ----------- |
{% for fname, f in t.fields | items -%}
| {{ t.fields | items | field_offset(loop.index0) }} | {{ fname | field_display(name) }} | {{ f | size_display }} | u{{ f.size }} | {{ f.doc | esc_md }} |
{% endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
